The two sides have been at odds for years over issues like salary cap and league-owned teams, but they’re now at a standstill, and an agreement isn’t expected until the new year at the earliest.
The league’s current season is scheduled to end March 2, but that doesn’t look likely if a season is starting without a new deal. The league’s board of governors and players association are now in arbitration to try to reach an agreement, and both are threatening legal action.
